title: Payers › Landing › Search, filter and open a payer
route: /payers
intro: The landing page is one calm card: a search box, three filters (state, insurance type, workflow status), a count line and one row per payer. A row shows the name and organization, the product and state, how many workflows are published and in draft, the date of the last update, whether the payer has a published workflow, and a mark when a rule change waits. The filters live in the address, so Back from a payer returns to the same list. The row or its name opens that payer's workspace.
dir: TD
---
start s1 "Look at the list under the page title\n'6 payers. The agents know how each one works.'"
screen card "Payers card\n'Search payers', 'All states', 'All insurance types',\n'Any workflow status', '6 payers · 3 with a change waiting'"
screen hd "Column heads (wide screens)\nPayer and organization, Product and state, Workflows,\nLast update, Status, Pending rule changes"
screen row "One row per payer, in the order\nOhio Medicaid, Commercial, Medicare Advantage, Behavioral carve-out\nName (link), organization under it when it differs,\nproduct and state, '2 published · 1 draft' or 'None yet',\nlast update (10/17), status pill, change mark"
process nar "On a narrow screen the same facts sit on two lines\nName and status pill, then product, state, workflows, update and mark"
decision dst "Does the payer have a published workflow?"
process st1 "Green pill 'Published'"
decision dst2 "Any draft?"
process st2 "Ochre pill 'Drafts only'"
process st3 "Grey pill 'No workflow'"
decision dwt "Is a rule change waiting for this payer?"
process wt1 "Ochre dot and 'Change waiting'"
process wt0 "Green dot, 'None' (narrow: 'No change waiting')"
process lu "Last update is the newest of\na saved workflow, a rule edit or a logged change\nShown as a date, 'None' when there is nothing"

input i1 "Type in 'Search payers'"
process sf "List narrows as you type\nMatches name, organization, product, state, plan type or group"
click c2 "Pick a state in 'State'\nAll states, then each state the payers are in"
click c3 "Pick an 'Insurance type'\nOhio Medicaid, Commercial, Medicare Advantage, Behavioral carve-out"
click c4 "Pick a 'Workflow status'\nHas a published workflow, Only drafts, No workflow"
process ad "The address holds the search and filters\n?q=, state=, type=, wf=\nChoosing 'All' clears that one"
process cnt "'3 of 6 payers · 3 with a change waiting'"
decision any "Does any payer still match?"
screen em "'No payer matches “text”.' or 'No payer matches these filters.'\nButton 'Clear filters'"
click clr "Click 'Clear filters'\n(also beside the filters once any is set)"
process clr2 "Search and filters reset\nEvery payer shows again"

click pk "Click a payer row, or its name"
process nav "Address becomes /payers/the-payer\nOpens the payer's workspace on Workflow Builder"
click ab "Click 'Add a payer'"
click bk "Back, or 'Payers' in the breadcrumb"
process bk2 "List returns with the same search and filters"
end e1 "The chosen payer's workspace is showing"
goto g1 "Continues in: Payers › Workspace › What the header says"
goto g2 "Continues in: Payers › Add a payer"
goto g3 "Continues in: Payers › Sites › Clinic-wide payers, drafts in view"

s1 --> card --> hd --> row --> nar
row --> dst
dst -->|Yes| st1 --> dwt
dst -->|No| dst2
dst2 -->|Yes| st2 --> dwt
dst2 -->|No| st3 --> dwt
dwt -->|Yes| wt1 --> lu
dwt -->|No| wt0 --> lu
card --> i1 --> sf --> ad
card --> c2 --> sf
card --> c3 --> sf
card --> c4 --> sf
ad --> cnt --> any
any -->|No| em --> clr --> clr2 --> row
any -->|Yes| pk
row --> pk --> nav --> e1
e1 --> bk --> bk2
nav --> g1
card --> ab --> g2
row -.-> g3
